From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:16:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] hk: keep a render's size non-zero when its render area is
 empty

An attachmentless pass takes its size from the render area. With an
empty area and a draw, hk sent width_px or height_px 0, which the kernel
refuses with EINVAL, and the client loses its device. hk already sends
1x1 for such a pass with no draws on G17P.

Counter-Strike 2 froze this way while loading a map: the rejected
submission held one 0x0 pass with no attachments among 64 commands.

Clamp the size sent to the kernel, not cr.width and cr.height: scissors
clamp to those, so a draw in the pass still covers nothing. A
fullscreen triangle in an empty area, with the API scissor at 16x16,
counts 0 fragment invocations.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 329cbc02d0ee5e6c6c8a8265d54baa0b187f933c)
---
 src/asahi/vulkan/hk_queue.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_queue.c b/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_queue.c
index 5ab808c69fb..4d3e6b9f3da 100644
--- a/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_queue.c
+++ b/src/asahi/vulkan/hk_queue.c
@@ -204,6 +204,11 @@ asahi_fill_vdm_command(struct hk_device *dev, struct hk_cs *cs,
       c->height_px = MIN2(c->height_px, cs->area_y1);
    }
 
+   /* An attachmentless pass takes its size from the render area, which can be
+    * empty, and the kernel refuses a zero dimension. */
+   c->width_px = MAX2(c->width_px, 1);
+   c->height_px = MAX2(c->height_px, 1);
+
    c->isp_bgobjdepth = cs->cr.isp_bgobjdepth;
    c->isp_bgobjvals = cs->cr.isp_bgobjvals;
 
